  "description": "Retention of the London Stadium as a multi-purpose sports, music, culture and community events venue with minor amendments to planning conditions relating to event restrictions set out in the extant planning permission (planning application reference 20/00060/VAR) In order to allow:\r- Increase in annual events from 10 to 24;\r- Increase maximum capacity for events to 85,000 for 8 events and maintain current capacity of 80,000 for 16 events;\r- Increase in consecutive nights of concerts from 3 to 4 (at a maximum of 4 occurrences per year);\r- Operate all events at a maximum music noise level of 75 dB;\r- Increase capacity for all sports events to 62,500 to match capacity for West Ham games;\r- Reduce annual frequency of sports events from 87 to 70; and\r- Include uniquely run sports events such as boxing and Soccer Aid within the definition for Events.",
